WEBVTT

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.130
Jeez, it's windy.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>Thank goodness the meeting ended early.</i>

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.340
<i>I might be able to leave on time today.</i>

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.450
<i>Maybe I'll take a break before 
heading back to the office.</i>

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:53.000
Koikimo

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.010
Episode 6

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.010
"Unrequited Love"

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:12.790
<b>Unkempt...</b>

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.190
My hair's a mess because of the wind.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.190
My makeup's
also a mess...

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.290
<i>I should at least try to look presentable...</i>

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.930
<i>It's not because Amakusa was sitting there.</i>

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.580
Pale Blue Nadeshiko

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.580
On air now!

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.580
The long-awaited anime version of the super popular shojo manga!

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.850
Oh, hey, Amakusa.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.090
What a coincidence. Are you on break?

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.760
Hey. Yeah, something like that.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.640
Are you ditching work?

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:43.240
Not quite. Just heading back from a meeting.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.140
I see.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.210
Thanks.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.150
Matsushima...

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.540
Huh? What?

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.110
You've got dead leaves on your coat.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.340
Huh?

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.280
You're right!

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.430
<i>Way to go, me...</i>

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.390
I should've checked everything...

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:10.190
<i>He's just doing work on his 
laptop at a café, and yet...</i>

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:13.090
<i>He shouldn't look this 
picture-perfect. It's not fair.</i>

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.540
Oh, yeah.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:15.990
Huh?

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.430
<i>Wait, did he see me staring?</i>

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.380
There's something I wanted 
to ask you, Matsushima.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.680
Sure, what is it?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.180
<b>Anime Updates!</b>

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.180
<b>New Spring Anime Lineup</b>

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.180
What are your anime 
recommendations for next season?

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:25.820
What?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.430
There are just too many. 
I don't know which ones to watch.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.870
So I wanted to ask for your input.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.960
<i>Assuming that Matsushima and 
Ichika-san's tastes are similar,</i>

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.530
<i>I can get a good guess on 
what anime she'll watch!</i>

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:45.950
<b>The
Calculating
Guy</b>

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.640
<i>Then I'll be able to check them early,</i>

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.950
<i>and I can have a lively 
discussion with Ichika-san!</i>

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:50.160
Are you looking up the anime for next season?

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:50.790
Yeah.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:54.780
What?

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.300
Sorry, I just wasn't expecting that.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:03.050
Let's see... Oh, I'd 
probably go with this one.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.050
<b>New Spring Anime Lineup</b>

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.050
OO-chan Back Drop

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.600
The original story was great, 
so I think it'd be easy to watch.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.450
<b>Whisper
Whisper...</b>

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:08.930
<b>Uh, you good?</b>

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.930
Why are you whispering?

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.590
Because someone else from 
the office might be here.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:14.560
Secret
Otaku

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.930
Oh... right.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.560
The office is close...

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.810
This, huh?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:17.210
Yeah...

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.070
OO-chan Back Drop

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.070
I see... Noted.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.040
Thanks.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:26.210
<i>Yeah, I think Amakusa might 
actually be pretty great.</i>

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.260
<i>He seems easier to talk to than before.</i>

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.620
I think I've seen this 
voice actor's name before.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.780
Besides, doesn't Amakusa have a girlfriend 
he's head over heels for right now?

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.920
Yeah, I think I heard that rumor.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.960
Something about an older girlfriend 
who works as a teacher?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.160
<i>Oh, right. That rumor's going around.</i>

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:46.470
<i>Wait...</i>

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.450
Yeah, I wasn't that interested.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:54.690
But someone I know is into anime, 
so I started watching because of them.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.620
<i>So is this person he mentioned 
actually his girlfriend?</i>

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.280
<i>Ah, it all makes sense now.</i>

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:05.160
<i>But I've only heard about said 
girlfriend through rumors.</i>

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.770
<i>It also seems like this rumor 
took a life of its own.</i>

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.220
<i>I want to get the facts 
from the actual source!</i>

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.950
<i>Should I? Should I?!</i>

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.350
There sure are a lot of idol anime series...

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:16.660
Say, Amakusa...

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:18.410
Do you have—

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.690
Sounds like you've got a message.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:22.710
Yeah...

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.520
<i>This timing...</i>

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:26.420
Oh.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.400
I've got a meeting, so I'm gonna head back.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.160
Sure.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.600
Jinguji

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.600
Hey!
We figured out when we're going 
drinking with work buddies!

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.600
It's going to be next Friday,
so if you know of anyone
to invite, go ahead!

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.320
Say, Amakusa!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.160
Next Friday, a bunch of us 
from work are going drinking.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:47.460
If you're not busy, would you like to come?

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.490
Next Friday...

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.330
That actually sounds fun.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.420
I'll check my schedule and get back to you.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.080
Okay.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.260
<i>Yes... Sweet!</i>

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:01.060
<i>Okay, I'll ask him about his 
girlfriend when we all go drinking!</i>

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.220
<i>I totally will!</i>

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.170
<b>Rustle</b>

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.840
Goodness, Ryo-kun. Are these for me?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:13.180
A
Different
Day

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:13.180
It may be a bit cliché, but since your name 
means "lily," I figured they'd be fitting.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.730
Oh, my!

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.320
Oh, and here's some pudding.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.520
I hope you all enjoy them.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:22.090
I said I'd walk,

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:24.130
Oh, my! Oh, who doesn't love clichés? 
And you even got us pudding!

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.040
but he insisted on driving me to your place.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:27.150
*Rio came to spend the night at Ichika's

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:25.760
I'm glad to hear it.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.170
Yeah, I had a feeling.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.910
Well, I hope my sister doesn't 
cause too much trouble.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:31.620
Thanks for having me over.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.220
Of course. Come on in, Rio-chan.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:38.610
Oh, Ryo-kun. Why not have some tea 
since you came all the way here?

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:39.290
What?!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:43.770
Oh, I'm sorry. I actually have 
to head to the office now.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.450
Oh, that's too bad.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:48.720
Okay, you heard him. 
Just get in the house, Mom!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:50.380
<b>Arima</b>

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.720
Hey!

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:49.500
Ichika-san.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.390
Yes?

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:04.620
Do you think it's okay if I ask Yuriko-san 
if I can also spend the night next ti—

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.420
Good luck with work! Bye!

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.990
<i>I hate how cowardly I am.</i>

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.140
<i>I should probably forget 
about asking Ichika-san</i>

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:19.370
<i>about what happened with 
Tamaru on their school trip.</i>

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.670
<i>If I'm going to waste time worrying,</i>

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.730
<i>I should spend that time trying to figure 
out how to make Ichika-san happy.</i>

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:30.170
<i>I barely get to see her as it is.</i>

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:33.250
<i>It'd be a waste if something was bugging 
me when I finally got to see her.</i>

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.300
<i>Though...</i>

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:40.390
<i>If something did indeed happen 
between Tamaru and Ichika-san...</i>

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:43.190
<i>I guess I'll have to deal with that, too.</i>

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:49.180
I'm just about to start cooking, 
so it'll be a little bit longer until dinner.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.270
Oh, I'll help, Yuriko-san.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:55.910
Why are you calling my mom by her name, too?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.020
Oh, really?

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.540
Then could you make the salad with Ichika?

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.400
Sure.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.910
Do you cook at home, Rio-chan?

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:07.040
Hm... I do prepare meals 
for myself quite often.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.800
Wow, that's impressive.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.180
My parents aren't home very often 
because of work, so I often eat alone.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.160
<i>Now that I think about it, I've been 
to Rio's place a bunch of times,</i>

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.930
<i>but I've never met her parents.</i>

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:23.010
You don't eat with Ryo-kun?

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:26.810
We eat together every once in a while 
when he's done with work early.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:31.010
I see. So who cooks when 
you two eat together?

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:35.450
My brother. Without a doubt, 
his dishes taste much better.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.990
Is it ready yet? I'm starving.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.040
Just set the plates and wait!

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.440
Yeah, I guess Ryo-san is a pretty good cook.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.170
You and your brother seem 
to get along pretty well.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.750
It was only recently that I started 
eating with my brother, though.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:54.600
He has his own place, and up until six 
months ago, he basically just stayed there.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.170
Wait, Ryo-san has his own place?

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.390
Yeah. It's close to his office.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.560
Oh, I see.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:02.890
<b>The upper floors
of a high-rise condo</b>

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:06.430
But he started coming back to our 
place more after he met you.

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:07.900
What? Why?

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.230
To get intel on you from me, duh.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:12.780
Oh, come on!

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:16.390
Also probably because our dad's 
living away from home for work now.

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:17.660
Your dad?

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:21.340
My dad and my brother <i>really</i> don't get along.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.410
They're like cats and dogs.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:25.250
I'm hom—

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.320
Don't give me that!

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:27.060
What?!

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:31.600
My dad's always been ridiculously 
hard on my brother.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:30.960
What could you possibly 
understand? You're just a child!

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.260
At least let me pick my own college!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.000
They would argue all the time.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.880
Why can't you just listen to me?!

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:41.000
I guess he got his own place so he 
wouldn't have to see our dad as much.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:45.770
I see... I guess you did 
mention your dad before, too.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:50.340
<i>He probably also got his own place 
so he could bring girls over,</i>

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.770
<i>but she doesn't need to know that.</i>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.170
<i>He hasn't been bringing any over lately.</i>

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:56.100
The cherry tomatoes are ready.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.740
Then do you mind if I add 
the finishing touches?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.360
Go ahead.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:03.320
On the other hand, my dad's 
not strict with me at all.

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:06.500
Does Ryo-kun get along with your mom?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:11.520
Oh, my mom and brother are totally fine. 
They talk to each other normally.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.630
So I guess it's just with your dad.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.680
<i>It's partly because my mom 
keeps asking questions,</i>

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.680
They're both so stubborn. It's such a pain.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.010
That must be rough.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:19.010
<i>but Rio's talking way more than usual.</i>

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:23.340
<i>I'm sure Rio's worried about 
her brother and father.</i>

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.090
<i>She doesn't really talk 
about that kind of stuff.</i>

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.640
Let's add some paprika 
and... Oh, prosciutto.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.960
<i>Oh, right. Of course.</i>

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:34.350
I guess you and Ryo-san really 
are siblings and family.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:35.910
Uh, did you forget suddenly?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:39.530
I guess I never really 
thought about it until now.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:44.160
Oh! Rio-chan's making roses out of 
the prosciutto! You're so talented.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.160
Oh, no. This is nothing.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:51.750
Oh, I wouldn't say that. Ichika's not 
that talented, and she's so clumsy.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:57.130
Like, when she was in kindergarten, 
she spilled juice on her brand new dress.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:56.370
Mommy, I spilled my juice!

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:57.130
Mommy,
I spilled my juice!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.090
Like, seriously, <i>right</i> after.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:00.180
Uh, Mom? That's when I was little!

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:04.110
Huh... Oh, but when someone passed 
Ichika the ball the other day in PE,

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:06.280
she caught it with her face.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:05.610
Ichika, the ball...

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.020
Wait, why are you joining in, Rio?!

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:11.090
Seriously, Ichika?!

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:11.850
And the other day,

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:12.750
Just stop already!

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.980
she had no idea she had worn 
her shoes on the wrong feet

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:17.210
Just stop already! And wait, why are you 
and my mom getting along so well?! Ugh!

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.430
until our morning classes were over.

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:18.220
You're just so clumsy.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:21.660
Wow, that was fun.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:23.560
Thanks for today, Ichika.

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:26.420
Rio, about what you were saying earlier...

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:28.980
About Ryo-san and your dad.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:34.660
Ah... yeah. I've been hoping forever 
that they'll get along someday.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:37.520
I see. I guess you would be worried.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:41.610
Wow, you fall asleep fast!

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:53.030
Koikimo

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:58.030
Koikimo

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.000
Zzz...

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.000
Zzz...

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:58.020
She fell asleep
in 3 minutes...

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:58.020
Zzz...

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.490
<b>Ball Game Tournament</b>

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.490
Time Table

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.490
Time

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.490
Pairing

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.490
<b><u>Girls' Basketball</u></b>

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.490
I guess we have 30 minutes until Rio's game.

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:12.510
We still have some time, 
so let's go cheer elsewhere.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:17.250
<b>Girls Basketball</b>

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:18.260
Thanks to Rio and Sacchan's help, 
our team keeps moving up the ranks.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:21.010
Well, they're both very good at sports.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.880
<b>Girls' Basketball</b>

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:25.320
Let's just give our all in 
cheering everyone else on.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:27.880
<b>Lost in the first round of badminton</b>

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:27.880
<b>The bad-at-sports pair</b>

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:27.880
We need to keep up with Satsuki and Rio.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:29.810
Oh?

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:34.060
It looks like our boys' soccer 
team is moving up the ranks, too.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.020
<b>Boys' Soccer</b>

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.020
You're right.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.300
I wonder if the semifinals started yet.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.950
Let's go cheer them on!

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:39.900
Sure.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.370
Ichika! Ruri!

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:51.040
Kai. Hey, Kai!

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:53.330
Congrats, my guy.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:53.930
Huh?

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.460
Look! Over in the cheering 
section. Over there.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.090
Arima's here.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.280
So what?

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:01.420
They're just about to start.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.500
You don't need to be embarrassed.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.880
Hey, perfect timing.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:08.350
You guys did hang out together at 
the aquarium on our school trip.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.860
So many people from our class 
are here to cheer them on.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:11.400
So, you guys official yet? Huh?

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:14.900
Hey, you two! Our game's about to start!

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.180
Come on, let's go.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.190
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.400
Hey, just so we're clear...

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.360
I haven't told Arima how I feel yet.

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:28.200
I'll tell you when that happens, 
so just stay quiet until then.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:34.100
<b>Badump...</b>

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.030
<i>Oh, God. He's so cool.</i>

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.810
Anyway, just concentrate 
on the game right now.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:35.130
Oh. Right.

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:36.980
You've got this!

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:37.730
It's starting.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:40.310
Kai!

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:43.150
Let's go!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.730
You've got this!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.730
Go!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.730
Kawaguchi!

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:52.920
Huh?

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:52.920
Um...

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.070
<i>Um...</i>

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.740
Tamaru-kun looks amazing out there.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.200
Right?!

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:11.450
I never thought he'd be good 
at sports. I'm sorta shocked.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.200
Tamaru's gonna be even more popular now.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.200
Ichika, did you know Tamaru was good at soccer?

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.640
Huh? Why are you asking me?

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.590
Well, you guys are close, right?

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.620
No... I had no idea.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.020
Yeah!

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:29.050
Way to go, Kai!

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:31.800
<i>Tamaru-kun really does look cool out there.</i>

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:33.470
Hey, Ichika.

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:38.250
You might have more rivals 
after the tournament today.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.730
Rivals? Huh? For what?

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:43.250
You know what I'm talking about.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.490
Wait, wait, wait. There's nothing 
going on between me and Tamaru-kun.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.240
Oh, really?

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.930
Yes, really!

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:53.490
<i>She thinks I'm just embarrassed to admit it.</i>

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.750
<i>I wonder if Ryo-san's good at soccer, too...</i>

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.750
You've got this! Go! Yeah! Shoot!

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.970
Isn't that great, Ichika?!

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:06.720
Huh? Yeah, it's great.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.940
They're going to the finals next!

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:10.300
That's amazing!

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.630
They might even win the whole thing!

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:13.300
They were up against 
third-years and still won.

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:15.200
I know! It's so exciting!

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:16.310
Yeah. I hope they win the whole thing.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:20.310
Oh, Rio and Satsuki's match is starting soon.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.190
Oh, we should head to the gym.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.700
Okay, we're gonna go cheer 
for the basketball team.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:26.290
Okay!

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:27.820
What'd you think, Kai?

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:31.240
Did you see that amazing long pass 
 I did? Aren't I awesome?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.010
You passed the ball to me way too much.

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:36.560
I was giving you the spotlight.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:42.490
<i>I sorta wanted to hear what 
she thought of the game.</i>

00:15:58.320 --> 00:15:59.580
They won!

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:12.820
Meanwhile,
the boys'
soccer team...

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:11.270
I guess you couldn't keep up 
without Arima's support.

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:12.820
lost in
the finals

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:12.820
That's not it!

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.330
<b>Izakaya</b>

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:20.060
He's definitely gonna be the most successful.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:22.270
Don't forget about me when you're famous.

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:24.500
What the heck?

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:33.260
I haven't had a chance to ask 
Amakusa about his girlfriend...

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:35.640
<i>That's not surprising, though.</i>

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:40.100
<i>We're all from different departments, 
so we're just talking about our departments.</i>

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:37.430
So, yeah, our sales guys...

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.100
Nah, just wait till you hear...

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:43.140
<i>It would be weird to just 
ask him out of the blue.</i>

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.750
Hey, there you are.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:49.770
We're thinking about wrapping things 
up here and going for round two—

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.170
Please! Help me out!

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:52.840
Huh?

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:55.110
All right.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:58.860
That about wraps up round one, so now...

00:16:58.860 --> 00:16:59.890
What about round two?

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:01.620
Yeah, sorry. I'm gonna peace out.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.430
Yeah, yeah. Better hurry home, you newlywed.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:06.020
Oh, right. He is.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:06.990
Shoo, shoo. Shoo, shoo.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.750
Could you sound any more bitter?

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:08.320
Damn newlywed.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.250
So...

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:12.260
You guys are coming to karaoke with me.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:16.060
You're coming and that's that! Now walk!

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:19.640
Amakusa!

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:24.320
I think Arrietty wants to drink 
a bit more, so keep her company.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.230
Okay, then!

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.570
Come on! Let's go!

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:30.110
Ugh, honestly, you drunks.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:33.350
Say, Amakusa...

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.870
There's a bar nearby that I wanted to visit.

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:42.370
Why don't we have a few more drinks there? 
It's sorta hard for me to go alone.

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:45.620
Yeah, sure. Let's go.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.240
Okay.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.070
<i>Yes!</i>

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:53.340
By the way, I've been wondering... 
Is "Arrietty" your nickname?

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:57.810
Yeah. My name's Arie, so my friends 
and coworkers call me that.

00:17:57.810 --> 00:17:59.580
Ah, I see.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:03.550
<i>I-It's super embarrassing 
having to explain my nickname!</i>

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.560
Matsushima
It worked out!!
Thanks!
I'll treat you to lunch soon!

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:09.220
Hell yeah!

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:16.930
So that sound we heard at the meeting was 
the section chief's stomach growling?

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:22.160
Yeah. I was sitting next to 
him, so it was super loud.

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:25.910
It echoed through the whole meeting room.

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:29.130
You were at a loss for 
words for a sec, Amakusa.

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:34.180
Well, you were laughing, too. I remember 
the papers you were holding were shaking.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:36.010
I guess you caught me.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:40.040
So, hey. Sorry to change the subject, but...

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:41.510
What's up?

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:44.280
I'm just gonna come out and ask.

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:47.520
Are the rumors about your girlfriend true?

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.120
Rumors about my girlfriend?

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:54.270
Y-You know. Something about her being 
older and a teacher... or something.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:59.370
Oh, that. How did that rumor even start?

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.740
<i>Wait, he's smiling?</i>

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.530
<i>Wh-What's that mean?</i>

00:19:05.430 --> 00:19:07.040
I don't have a girlfriend like that.

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:09.790
Oh, really?

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:14.250
That rumor seemed to start out of nowhere.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:16.920
No one ever asked me about it, 
so I didn't say anything.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.380
I see...

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.630
Hm?

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.630
Basically the reason
the rumor spread

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.480
So do you have a girlfriend right now?

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:23.390
Nah.

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:24.700
<i>He doesn't have one.</i>

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:26.810
<i>Meaning... he's single!</i>

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:29.650
<i>Wait a sec! I think I can 
actually get my hopes up.</i>

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:31.390
I do have a crush, though.

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:35.420
A crush?

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:36.330
Yeah.

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:39.780
Oh... Huh. I see.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:43.030
Just going out on a limb here...

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:47.910
but is this person you know 
who likes anime... your crush?

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.600
Well, aren't you sharp?

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:50.910
Yup, you're correct.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:55.200
Oh, despite how I got into anime, 
I do actually like it now.

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:58.050
It's okay. I didn't doubt that.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.050
It's just...

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:05.480
Whenever she talks about anime, 
she looks a lot like you, Matsushima.

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:07.630
Episode 8? OMG, I know, right?!

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:10.760
The first-press limited 
edition Blu-ray?! Wait, why?!

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.050
Huh...

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:15.810
<i>I don't think I want to hear the rest.</i>

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:17.810
I do have a crush, though.

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:20.540
<i>Hm? A crush?</i>

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:27.230
Hey, sorry to pry, but this is basically 
unrequited love on your part, right?

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:28.950
Yeah, it is.

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:32.750
What?

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:33.620
<i>Then...</i>

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.750
<i>Then I think I still have a chance.</i>

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:38.960
<i>We're sorta alike, right? In that case...</i>

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.250
What's wrong? What did 
you want to drink next?

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:41.650
<i>That means I still have a chance, right?!</i>

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:44.790
<i>Right?!</i>

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.540
You had quite a bit to drink, 
but you seem totally fine.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:52.060
Yeah, I can handle my liquor pretty well.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.560
Hey, thanks for inviting me out tonight.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.750
Everyone was really happy you came, Amakusa.

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.710
Hanging out like that every 
now and then is fun.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:03.950
We're probably going to do 
it again next month or so.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.580
You should come again.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:06.780
Yeah.

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:09.550
Well, I'm gonna go...

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:14.790
What is it?

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:17.720
No, it's nothing.

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:24.760
Thanks for walking me to the 
station. I'll see you later.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:26.170
Yeah, later.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:29.720
This is basically unrequited 
love on your part, right?

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:43.900
Hello, it's Ryo. I'm sorry 
to call you so late.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:46.040
Huh?

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:51.130
I just suddenly wanted to hear your voice.

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:56.600
Just like usual? I guess you could say that.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:03.420
<i>"How to make a guy who's in love 
with someone else notice you..."</i>

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:06.260
How to make a guy who's in love with someone else notice you

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:06.260
Ways to make a guy who's in love with someone else notice you

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:05.080
<i>And search!</i>

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
Next Time

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
"Love for Your Fave"

00:23:36.030 --> 00:23:38.410
Next time, "Love for Your Fave."
